    "text": "An electric field <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>C</mi></math> passes through the box shown in figure. The flux of the electric field through surfaces <math><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi></math> and <math><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>G</mi><mi>F</mi></math> are marked as <math><msub><mrow><mi>&#981;</mi></mrow><mrow><mtext>I</mtext></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>&#981;</mi></mrow><mrow><mtext>II</mtext></mrow></msub></math> respectively. The difference between <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>&#981;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mrow><mi>&#981;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> is (in <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> ) ____________.<br /><br /><img src=\"assets\\qt0186_517e3492c347.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 236px;\" />"
